  "flavor": {
    "races": {
      "Human": "Versatile and tenacious, humans spread across Golarion faster than any other people, adapting to every land they claim.",
      "Elf": "Long-lived folk of fading forests and arcane grace. Elves remember centuries most others have forgotten.",
      "Dwarf": "Mountain-born craftsmen bound by clan and oath. A dwarf's word is a promise carved in stone.",
      "Halfling": "Small, cheerful, and quietly fearless. Halflings wander the world with a knack for luck and a talent for not being noticed.",
      "Gnome": "Endlessly curious souls who fade if they stop seeking wonder. Gnomes chase color, music, and novelty with infectious energy.",
      "Orc": "Strength and endurance forged by hardship. Orcs carry the weight of a harsh past and turn it into unbreakable resolve.",
      "Goblin": "Chaos with a heartbeat. Goblins burn bright and loud, devouring life — and occasionally their own inventions.",
      "Leshy": "Plant-bodied spirits given form by a druid's hand. Each leshy is grown for a purpose and shaped by the seasons.",
      "Tengu": "Crowlike wanderers and collectors. Tengu flock together, hoarding stories, steel, and secrets in equal measure.",
      "Catfolk": "Graceful amurrun traders and travelers, curious by nature and quick on every surface, nine lives not guaranteed."
    },
    "classes": {
      "Alchemist": "A brewer of bombs, elixirs, and happy accidents. Alchemists turn the periodic table into a battle plan.",
      "Barbarian": "Fury is their heritage and their weapon. A barbarian's rage transforms pain into devastating power.",
      "Bard": "A silver-tongued artist whose magic lives in performance. Bards inspire allies and disarm enemies with a verse.",
      "Champion": "A holy bulwark sworn to a cause. Champions stand between the innocent and the darkness, shield raised.",
      "Cleric": "A vessel of divine will. Clerics call down their deity's power as healing mercy or radiant judgment.",
      "Druid": "A steward of the primal world. Druids command the elements, the wilds, and the very shape of their own body.",
      "Fighter": "Mastery of combat above all else. fighters turn every battlefield into an expression of disciplined skill.",
      "Gunslinger": "A dead-eye whose every shot tells a story. Gunslingers gamble on powder, timing, and one perfect moment.",
      "Inventor": "A genius with a devoted, half-mad device at their side. Inventors build impossible machines and overclock them.",
      "Investigator": "A deductive mind that sees patterns others miss. Investigators out-think danger before the first blow lands.",
      "Kineticist": "A living conduit of elemental power. Kineticists channel fire, water, earth, air, or wood as an extension of self.",
      "Magus": "Sword in one hand, spell in the other. Magi fuse steel and sorcery into a single devastating strike.",
      "Monk": "A disciplined artist of unarmed combat. Monks perfect the body into a weapon and the mind into armor.",
      "Oracle": "A martyr cursed with divine power. Oracles know the future and pay for it with a burden no prayer can lift.",
      "Psychic": "A mind whose thoughts reshape reality. Psychics manifest raw mental power as bolts, shields, and subtle control.",
      "Ranger": "A hunter attuned to the wild and the hunt. Rangers track, trap, and strike where the enemy least expects.",
      "Rogue": "A shadow with a hundred tricks. Rogues slip past every lock and guard, then strike where it truly hurts.",
      "Sorcerer": "Magic burns in their bloodline. Sorcerers shape inherited power by instinct rather than study.",
      "Summoner": "Bound by spirit to an eidolon. Summoners and their otherworldly partner fight as one perfect, synced whole.",
      "Swashbuckler": "Duelist, braggart, and whirlwind of style. Swashbucklers turn panache into punctuation and every duel into a story.",
      "Thaumaturge": "A collector of relics and true names. Thaumaturges wield symbol and story to wound the strange and esoteric.",
      "Witch": "Patron-bound keeper of hexes and familiars. Witches bargain with mysterious powers and whisper their curses to the world.",
      "Wizard": "The scholar supreme. Wizards master reality through discipline, study, and an ever-growing spellbook."
    }
  },
